{"name":"Penelope","hex":"#e3e3eb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Penelope","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Cracidae – typical guans, 65 to 95 cms in length, of the Neotropics."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The faithful wife of Odysseus.","A female given name from Ancient Greek."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Penelope"}],"entries":[{"title":"Penelope","blocks":[{"text":"Penelope is the legendary wife of Odysseus and queen of Ithaca in Homer's Odyssey. She is the daughter of Spartan king Icarius, and the mother of Telemachus. Different sources describe her as the mother of figures such as Poliporthes, Arcesilaus, Italus, Mamilia, and the god Pan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Exposition_Paris-Ath%C3%A8nes_au_Mus%C3%A9e_du_Louvre_%C3%A0_Paris_-parisathenes_%2851544789732%29.jpg/330px-Exposition_Paris-Ath%C3%A8nes_au_Mus%C3%A9e_du_Louvre_%C3%A0_Paris_-parisathenes_%2851544789732%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penelope","wikidata":"Q165769"},{"title":"Penelope (2006 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Penelope is a 2006 fantasy romantic comedy film directed by Mark Palansky and starring Christina Ricci, James McAvoy, Catherine O'Hara, Peter Dinklage, Richard E. Grant, and Reese Witherspoon. The film tells the story of a young heiress named Penelope Wilhern, who was born with the snout of a pig due to a curse that was placed on her family by a vengeful witch, believing the only way to break the curse is to find another blue blood who truly loved her."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f9/Penelope_Poster_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penelope_(2006_film)","wikidata":"Q1074032"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm